# Honest Learn server settings. Copy this file to ".env" in the same folder and edit it.
#   Windows:  copy .env.example .env        macOS/Linux:  cp .env.example .env
# Then start the server with:  node --env-file=.env --import tsx src/preview.ts   (or see docs/FREE_AGENTS.md)
# Never commit your .env file or share your keys. (.env is already ignored by git.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Hoot, the AI helper: pick ONE option

# Option 1: no AI at all (the default). Hoot answers with each lesson's own pre-written hints.
# TUTOR_MODE=mock

# Option 2: a free model on your own computer with Ollama (https://ollama.com). No key, nothing leaves the computer.
#   Install Ollama, then run:  ollama pull llama3.2
# TUTOR_MODE=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.2

# Option 3: any other OpenAI-compatible service (LM Studio, OpenRouter, Groq, Together, OpenAI, ...)
# TUTOR_MODE=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=your-key-here
# LLM_MODEL=the-model-name
# LLM_SAFETY_MODEL=a-stronger-model-for-the-second-check   (optional; defaults to LLM_MODEL)
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=60000                                      (optional; raise it for slow computers)

# Option 4: Claude (the only option tested with this project's safety test set)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here

# Families can also pick their own model in the app (Parent area > Account > Hoot's AI). That choice wins for that family.
# AI_KEY_SECRET=a-long-random-string   # encrypts the keys families save there; set it on any real server. Changing it makes saved keys unreadable.
# ALLOW_LOCAL_LLM=true                 # lets families use a model on this computer or the home network (always off on Vercel)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional
# TUTOR_DAILY_LIMIT=40        # Hoot messages per child per day
# PORT=3000
